# authorized_keys options of the laptop's forwarding-only tunnel key
# (~/.ssh/oryx-tunnel on the laptop). On oryx, this line goes in front of that
# key's public line in agent's ~/.ssh/authorized_keys. permitlisten lists the
# ports the laptop's RemoteForwards open on oryx's loopback, permitopen the oryx
# channels its LocalForwards reach, and the forced command gives the key no
# shell. Where a RemoteForward ends on the laptop's side is the laptop's own
# choice, which sshd cannot see or limit. permitopen also refuses a LocalForward
# to a Unix socket, but nothing here limits a RemoteForward that listens on a
# socket path on oryx (OpenSSH 9.6, scratch sshd, 2026-11-13), so sshd on
# oryx's port 2222 must also set AllowStreamLocalForwarding no.
restrict,port-forwarding,permitlisten="127.0.0.1:12800",permitlisten="127.0.0.1:12803",permitlisten="127.0.0.1:12804",permitlisten="127.0.0.1:12806",permitlisten="127.0.0.1:5038",permitlisten="127.0.0.1:2223",permitlisten="127.0.0.1:2224",permitopen="127.0.0.1:12801",permitopen="127.0.0.1:12802",permitopen="127.0.0.1:12805",command="echo oryx-tunnel: forwarding-only key"
